{{~##
Image Helpers - Lumina Theme

Responsive-image functions shared by every partial that renders a <picture>
(Image, ContentImage, PhotoLightbox, OpenGraphImage, Body/Photo), so their
markup cannot drift apart. Include this partial before calling them; it renders
nothing itself.

- image_type format         MIME type for <source type>: "jpg" -> "image/jpeg"
- image_fallback_format     The last of image_formats (normally "jpg"), for the <img> fallback
- image_srcset image format Every generated size as "url <width>w" candidates
- image_size image limit    Largest generated size up to limit, else the smallest
- viewer_sizes image        `sizes` for a photo fitted into the photo viewer

image.sizes lists the generated sizes in ascending order. A size is the longest
edge (images.json "resizeMode": "longest"), so portrait candidates are narrower.
##~}}
{{~ func image_type(format)
    ret 'image/' + (format == 'jpg' ? 'jpeg' : format)
end ~}}
{{~ # image_formats is a plain collection without an index, so take its last item by looping. ~}}
{{~ func image_fallback_format
    for $format in image_formats
        $last = $format
    end
    ret $last
end ~}}
{{~ func image_srcset(image, format)
    $srcset = ''
    for $size in image.sizes
        $width = image.width >= image.height ? $size : $size * image.width // image.height
        $srcset = $srcset + ($srcset == '' ? '' : ', ') + (variant_url image $size format) + ' ' + $width + 'w'
    end
    ret $srcset
end ~}}
{{~ func image_size(image, limit)
    $best = image.sizes[0]
    for $size in image.sizes
        if $size <= limit; $best = $size; end
    end
    ret $best
end ~}}
{{~ # The viewer fits the photo into the viewport above the photo navigation bar. ~}}
{{~ func viewer_sizes(image)
    ret '(min-aspect-ratio: ' + image.width + '/' + image.height + ') calc((100vh - 2.25rem) * ' + image.width + ' / ' + image.height + '), 100vw'
end ~}}
